{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"# Session: cut Gerrit Verified gate wall-clock without losing coverage\n\n## Question\n\"How can we reduce the wall-clock runtime of our Gerrit Verified Gate on GitHub Actions\nwithout reducing our coverage?\" Operator later reported real gate times of 41-47 min.\n\n## What the measurements showed\n- Critical path was ONE job: `pytest (macos-latest, py3.13)` at 18.6m (run #1823 /\n  id 30569775555). Every other job <=8m; without macOS the run finishes in ~8m.\n- Within it: setup 0.7m, twelve drift gates ~0.1m, default pytest tier 15.4m, integration 2.0m.\n- 7856 tests: ubuntu 5:04 at -n 4 vs macOS 15:21 at -n 3 — a 3x wall gap against a 1.33x vCPU gap.\n- Dispatch lag from Gerrit is NOT a factor: change 1052 ps1 uploaded 18:24:36, run created\n  18:24:38 (2s), Verified+1 at 18:53:35 = 29.0m, matching GitHub's own run_duration_ms.\n- THE BINDING CONSTRAINT: navapbc is on GitHub Free = 20 concurrent jobs / 5 macOS,\n  enforced PER ORGANIZATION, shared with every other navapbc repo. A single Verified run\n  needs 21 job slots — one run alone cannot fully parallelize. Six changes dispatched within\n  10 seconds queued 6.7-8.4m each for a macOS slot. That queue is the 41-47m.\n- Peak concurrent macOS jobs observed across 25 sampled jobs: 4, never more.\n\n## What landed (5 changes, all merged, all tickets closed)\n| Change | Ticket | Effect |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1056 | f3d4 | coverage collected on ubuntu cells only (measured +5.1% overhead, so ~0.8m) |\n| 1063 | 699f | store template + copy-per-test: tests/interfaces 270.7s -> 186.5s at -n 4 (31%) |\n| 1065 | 2132 | deleted redundant import-linter job, repaid with a durable collection guard |\n| 1066 | ad63 | optionality fan-out 6 jobs -> 1 venv loop (7 iterations, 7 venvs) |\n| 1070 | 446c | template-virginity assertion moved into the fixture |\n\nCoverage went UP, not down: `metrics` is in `_optional.EXTRAS` but had NO per-extra CI\nbefore 1066; the loop now covers it.\n\n## Rejected, with reasons (do not re-propose without new evidence)\n- **3-way macOS shard.** `fail_under = 70` is enforced PER pytest session, so every shard\n  fails (reproduced: 26.91% on a 4% subset). `.test_durations` is gitignored deliberately by\n  ticket 9ad9. The `pytest-split` dep in pyproject was a WAIVED scope-creep finding against\n  ticket 8d36, not prior intent. Honest speedup 2.2x not 3x, and it RAISES macOS job-minutes\n  18.6 -> 21.0, making the 6-run burst worse (22.3 -> 25.2m). Wins only when R x S <= C, i.e.\n  one solitary change.\n- **macOS `-n 3 -> 4`.** The IO-bound premise was wrong: serial CPU:wall is 0.71, `-n 3`\n  already demands 2.19 of 3 vCPUs, scaling saturates at `-n 6` and REGRESSES at `-n 9` on an\n  18-core box, with sys > user throughout (kernel/filesystem contention). Its stated\n  precondition (widen tests/scripts/reducer/test_reducer_cache.py:288) targets a test that is\n  `skipif(CI == \"true\")` and never runs in CI. Worth re-deriving now that 1063 removed ~58\n  process spawns per interfaces test, since that changes the sys/user balance it rested on.\n\n## Load-bearing facts discovered (cite these, don't re-derive)\n- **The Verified gate CANNOT exercise a change to `.github/workflows/**`.** `uses:\n  ./.github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml` resolves from the DEFAULT BRANCH under\n  workflow_dispatch; the patchset is only checked out INSIDE jobs. A flat pre-merge number is\n  not evidence a workflow change did nothing — verified by dumping the macOS command line on\n  1056's own run and finding `--cov` still present.\n- **The working pre-merge lane for workflow changes is a SCRATCH BRANCH push to the mirror**\n  (`optionality.yml` triggers on push, branches-ignore feature/**). A PULL REQUEST does not\n  work: `.github/workflows/lockdown.yml` runs repo-lockdown on pull_request_target with\n  close-pr: true. Used successfully on 1066 (run 30591336796).\n- **Bare `git worktree repair` is DESTRUCTIVE, not a silent no-op.** Run inside a copy it\n  rewrites the SOURCE's `.tickets-tracker/.git` to point into the copy.\n- **`--git-common-dir` is green on a half-fixed store copy.** It derives from\n  `.tickets-tracker/.git` alone and cannot witness a stale `gitdir`. Use\n  `git worktree list --porcelain` containment.\n- **`conftest` is not a stable module name.** Several conftests share it; under xdist\n  `sys.modules[\"conftest\"]` binds to whichever was imported last. `from conftest import X`\n  works when a tier runs alone and fails in a full-suite run. Hence\n  `tests/interfaces/_store_template.py`.\n- **`init._gen_local_files()` is idempotency-guarded** (`if not os.path.isfile`), so calling\n  it to re-mint `.env-id`/`.signing-key` on a copy is a silent no-op.\n- **The gate snapshot store is keyed by COMMIT SHA ALONE** (`_snapshot/repo_snapshot.py`), so\n  a shared template SHA collapses ~150 gate-touching tests onto one entry. `REBAR_GATE_TMPDIR`\n  is set per test.\n- **`_optional.EXTRAS` != the old per-extra matrix list.** EXTRAS = {agents, eval, grounding,\n  metrics, tracing}; `mcp` is NOT in it (no probe; validated by its boot check).\n- **The literal `|| { rc=1; ...; continue; }` accumulator trips shellcheck SC2015** through\n  actionlint and fails `make lint`. Use `if ! { ...; }; then ...; fi`.\n\n## Process notes\nFive review rounds each found something real; two layers caught different classes — rebar's\nplan gate found unproven ACs and a false factual claim, subagents found mechanism bugs.\nMy own recurring error: asserting a safety property in the ACs while the mechanism I specified\ncould not deliver it (a `--git-common-dir` guard that passes on the broken case; a\n`list_tickets`-based isolation check that reads worktree files, not refs; a claimed PR\nvalidation lane that auto-closes). Validating 1063 by running `tests/interfaces` alone was the\none scope where its bug was invisible — the full suite caught it.\n\n## Left open\n- `docs/llm-framework.md` \"The optional surface is three extras\" is stale: `_optional.EXTRAS`\n  has five. Needs new descriptive content for `grounding` and `metrics` — separate ticket.\n- Deferred from 699f: ~20 module-local fixtures in tests/interfaces still build stores the old\n  way. Migrating them onto `_clone_template` is the larger remaining share of that win."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785459391440138001,"uuid":"3c366059-7824-4be7-bf98-a97ce8342b5e"}